# Kid Loki: "Whenever you draw your second card each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Kid Loki" and "Each creature you control that
# you've put one or more +1/+1 counters on this turn has hexproof." In turn 3 the draw step's card is Bot1's first and Opt's is
# the second: Kid Loki gets the counter (a 2/2) and, for the rest of that turn, hexproof: Bot2 cannot target it with Lightning
# Bolt at the end step (the refusal). In Bot2's turn 4 the counter was put "this turn" no longer, so the Bolt can: it kills the 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Kid Loki
Opt
Island
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kid Loki.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Opt.Cast
Bot1.Arrange(Island |)
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki.Keywords = Hexproof
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki)
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Kid Loki; Opt
